title an escape above 377 names no byte

# Three octal digits reach 511; a byte does not.
#
# This case spent a round in devcheck/pending/ because the two
# parsers disagreed, and it is the best thing the cross-parser diff
# has caught. The reference accepted \400 and built a character with
# code 256 -- not a byte -- which re-encoded to "\400" in the dump
# and so looked entirely correct. A value that survives a round trip
# and is still wrong is the worst shape a bug can take. In C the same
# escape truncates to NUL, smuggling in the one byte the NUL check
# exists to reject.
#
# Both parsers reject it now, in the same words.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: over\400flow
